
!set name_intro=is a visual game/exercise. It presents you two shapes, \
  one being the image of the other after a rotation in the plane.\
  And you are asked to find out the center of the rotation\
  by clicking on the picture.

!distribute lines Difficulty level\
  Number of clicks in one session\
  A score will be given at the end of a session\
  Here is your reply, as well as the real rotation center.\
  red,original shape\
  green, rotated shape\
  where you have clicked,the center of rotation\
  Average precision of the session\
  Continue with a new shoot\
  Start a new session\
  Reconfigure the game\
  Score\
  Résumé of the shots of the session\
into name_introlevel, name_introcount, name_introscore,\
  name_answer,name_red,name_green,name_answer2,name_ecart2,\
  name_next,name_again, name_configure, name_score,name_resume

!set name_present=Here you see two shapes in different colors. \
  One is produced from the other by a rotation in the plane. \
  Find the center of this rotation.

!set name_consigne=To give your reply: click in the figure, at the place\
  where you think is the good one.

!set name_ecart=!nosubst Precision of the reply (number $reply_cnt on $shoots):

!set name_end=!nosubst End of the session with $reply_cnt shots. Average precision
!set name_help=The center of the rotation is a point whose distance towards\
  a point and its rotated image is the same.
